For today’s class, Elio gave us a lecture about ideation. This lecture would then help the class to brainstorm for our projects.
We grabbed a big piece of paper and spent about 20 minutes writing down the most important things for our project such as the client’s goal, 
research about the islands, and resources.

Once that was done, we discussed about it and took a new sheet of paper for the next step. 
This time, we jotted down our questions, our concerns, cool features we wanted to include, and visual ideas, like colors, styles, 
and layouts to help create what our final project could look like.
        
